From: Armada contributors <noreply@armada-os.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-dai: allow 32-bit PCM playback

Allow an S32_LE playback topology to open and pass its sample width to
the existing AudioReach PCM configuration path. The Duo speaker topology
uses 32-bit samples throughout to match the AW88166 firmware's slots.
Without this capability, ALSA rejects the S32_LE frontend at open.
Keep capture capabilities unchanged.

Speaker output was confirmed after a clean boot on the Duo with the
matching S32_LE topology and primary MI2S backend format.

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -113,7 +113,8 @@
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_PAUSE |
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_NO_REWINDS | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_SYNC_APPLPTR |
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH),
-	.formats =              (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE),
+	.formats =              (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |
+				 SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE),
 	.rates =                SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000_192000,
 	.rate_min =             8000,
 	.rate_max =             192000,
@@ -537,6 +538,9 @@
 		break;
 	case SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S24_LE:
 		prtd->bits_per_sample = 24;
+		break;
+	case SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE:
+		prtd->bits_per_sample = 32;
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
